  {
   "evidence": "Tarski.lean:247-249 is `apply sum_sign h hseed ?_ hab ha hb; intro r _ _ hr; exact hp.eval_derivative_ne_zero hr`, i.e. exactly the instantiation a caller would write. `grep -rn \"sum_sign_of_squarefree\" code/TauCeti` returns only the declaration site (Tarski.lean:240), and `grep -rn \"eval_derivative_ne_zero\" code/TauCeti` shows its sole use is Tarski.lean:249 inside this wrapper.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Polynomial/Sturm/Tarski.lean",
   "fix": "Delete `sum_sign_of_squarefree`; callers pass `fun r _ _ hr => hp.eval_derivative_ne_zero hr` to `sum_sign` (keeping the reusable bridge `Squarefree.eval_derivative_ne_zero`, TauCeti/Algebra/Polynomial/Squarefree.lean:27), and note the squarefree consequence in `sum_sign`'s docstring instead.",
   "issue": "`sum_sign_of_squarefree` (240-249) has the same conclusion and same chain/seed/endpoint hypotheses as `sum_sign` (222-237), only replacing the pointwise `hsimple` by `Squarefree p`; its whole body is a one-line instantiation and it has no consumer, so it duplicates `sum_sign`'s public surface. No analogous squarefree variant exists for `card_roots`, `sum_sign_sturmSeq`, or the Ioi/Iio/univ family, so it is also an isolated entry point.",
   "line": "240"
  }
 ],
